s:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T18:03:01-07:00","id":161290,"title":"","content":"Nothing has changed for our license so far as we've heard. Still rolling right along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:01:01-07:00","id":163927,"title":"","content":"<br /> I knew, or at least believed, the license would be fine. But with the former WW staffers out of work (or at last let go from WW), then Onyx Path has a pool of talent they already know - and OP could hardly be blamed for hiring known talents for a job. To put it another way, when the unfortunate closure of WW more or less created a pool of known talented and available writers, so is there even a point to the writer all call for unknown writers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T04:07:20-07:00","id":1321496,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a very interesting post! I love reading different opinions. I work for <a href=\"https://expertwriter.net\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.expertwriter.net</a> as an editor, and I love reading lots of articles for enhance my knowledge. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"useri